{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0168482ABXZMwYtNNqyBtXfR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me summarize what I know:\n\n**Paper**: \"OntoCoDec: Universal Ontology-Constrained Structured Generation for Information Extraction\"\n\n**Core idea**: A framework that compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers for decoding-time enforcement:\n1. Grammar layer (CFG via XGrammar) - structural validity and vocabulary membership\n2. Semantic layer (stateful entity registry with dynamic logit masking) - domain/range and role-argument type constraints\n\n**Key findings**:\n- LLMs violate ontology constraints at 6.5-26% for domain/range, up to 89% for role vocabulary\n\n\n- The semantic layer depends on the grammar layer being enforced first, and together they validate across multiple tasks, models, and datasets\n- Post-hoc filtering would discard a significant portion of predictions, though cross-field violations represent an inherent tradeoff in the approach\n\nNow I'm setting up the review process by preparing detailed prompts for two reviewers—one focused on methods and experiments, another on novelty and related work—making sure they're blind to any tier information before running them in parallel.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17116,"cache_read_input_tokens":45220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17116},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0eddf8e3-65e4-4850-9e66-a5c0b106b0fa","uuid":"f71101fb-6542-4336-b17a-01fcdac52a86"}
