{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLj3NK1z7x5xfH3ushMcrX","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/_project/paper/section1_introduction_draft.tex:32:    \\item Empirical validation on 3 models $\\times$ 3 datasets (2 RE + 1 EE): DR $\\downarrow$76--99\\% on SciERC and $\\downarrow$42--90\\% on DocRED with significant R-F1 gains (Qwen $p{<}0.001$, Llama $p{=}0.013$); cross-task generalization to WikiEvents (vocabulary violations $\\to$\\,0\\%; Entity F1 0\\%\\,$\\to$\\,12--18\\%); composability with LoRA (DR\\,$\\leq$\\,0.20\\% at $<$0.6\\,pp F1 cost).\nartifacts/_project/paper/main.tex:77:Residual DR under fine-tuning (36 violations across all fine-tuned settings, both models and both datasets) decomposes into entity type errors (39\\%), schema coverage gaps (33\\%), and model generation errors correctly caught by constraints (28\\%); Llama DocRED alone accounts for 33 of 36 residual violations (92\\%), reflecting weaker entity typing (Appendix~\\ref{app:residual-dr-analysis}).\nartifacts/_project/paper/section5_scierc_draft.tex:118:Across all settings, fine-tuned + S1 yields DR\\,$\\leq$\\,0.20\\% with R-F1 within $\\pm$0.6\\,pp, which supports orthogonal composability."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019KGHhiAJcq4YrCimzrvPb7","session_id":"0eddf8e3-65e4-4850-9e66-a5c0b106b0fa","uuid":"0c4ae133-bb37-4b04-942f-3d1f29eb1a02","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:14:06.412Z"}
